 "source": "battle_fx.png",
 "notes": [
  "battle_fx.png is an object sheet on flat navy (measured 7,19,30). The glows and the dice are cut with darkkey, keeping their soft falloff; the game draws the three glows (impact, slash, dodge) additively, so their dark fringes add nothing. The two pieces with a navy interior -- the DEFEAT cloth and the round plate -- are cut rect and cleared outside their outline, as the guide asks of dark-interior plates.",
  "Rects are each object's ink grown by ~6 px of clean ground, found by labelling pixels more than 14 away from the ground and dilating.",
  "battle/impact and battle/slash replace the old generated 256x256 textures of the same names; the level-up ceremony's turning glow is battle/impact too, so it now wears the painted burst.",
  "battle/round_plate is no longer cut: the battle is drawn on art/reference/battle.png (art/slices/battle.json), whose own ROUND plate carries the round number."
